<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algerian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">ended <a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Algerian War was the war of independence fought by Algerian nationalists, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a>, against French rule from 1954 until it ended in 1962. It involved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare, urban terrorism, counter-insurgency and widespread use of torture. It caused a political crisis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and ended with Algerian independence, a major blow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algerian-war.jpg" alt="Algerian War" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zdravko Pečar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Liberation_Army_Soldiers_(7).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
